---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

const updated = 'September 30, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description={`How ${SITE.name}'s website collects and uses information.`}>
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-sky/60 to-paper">
    <div class="container-site max-w-3xl py-14 sm:py-20">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-5xl font-medium">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container-site max-w-3xl pb-20">
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif prose-headings:font-medium prose-a:text-clay">
      <p>
        This policy explains what information mjkalous.com (“the site”) collects, why, and the choices you have. In
        short: I collect only what's needed to send you the newsletter you ask for, answer your messages, and understand
        which pages are helpful. I never sell your information.
      </p>

      <h2 id="newsletter">Newsletter (Kit)</h2>
      <p>
        When you subscribe, your first name and email address are sent to <a href="https://kit.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Kit<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
        (formerly ConvertKit), the service that delivers the newsletter. Kit stores this information on my behalf and
        records basic engagement such as whether an email was opened. See
        <a href="https://kit.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Kit's privacy policy<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>To unsubscribe</strong>, click the “Unsubscribe” link at the bottom of any newsletter email. You'll be
        removed immediately. You can also email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and I'll remove you by
        hand.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact-form">Contact form</h2>
      <p>
        When you use the contact form, your name, email address, and message are delivered to my inbox through
        <a href="https://resend.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Resend<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>, an email delivery service. They're used only to reply to you.
        Please don't include sensitive health information; this form is not a secure channel for counseling and does not
        create a counselor–client relationship.
      </p>

      <h2 id="analytics">Google Analytics 4</h2>
      <p>
        If you click “Accept” on the cookie banner, the site loads Google Analytics 4, which uses cookies to collect
        information such as the pages you visit, how long you stay, your approximate location (city level), device and
        browser type, and how you arrived at the site. I use this only in aggregate to learn which writing is helpful.
        Google processes this data under its own <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
        You can also opt out across all sites with the
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out add-on<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="meta-pixel">Meta Pixel</h2>
      <p>
        If you accept cookies, the site also loads the Meta (Facebook) Pixel. It records visits and actions such as
        subscribing or clicking through to buy the book, so I can measure whether posts and ads on Facebook and Instagram
        are reaching the right people. Meta may link this activity to your Facebook or Instagram account under its own
        <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>. You can manage this in your
        <a href="https://www.facebook.com/adpreferences" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Meta ad preferences<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="videos">Embedded videos</h2>
      <p>
        Some pages include YouTube videos. Nothing is loaded from YouTube until you press play. When you do, the video
        plays through YouTube's privacy-enhanced mode (youtube-nocookie.com), and Google processes your viewing under its
        own <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="cookies">Your cookie choices</h2>
      <p>
        No analytics or advertising cookies are set unless you accept them. You can change your choice at any time:
        <a href="#" data-consent-reset>open cookie preferences</a>. Clearing your browser's site data will also reset it.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted by <a href="https://vercel.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vercel<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>, which keeps standard server logs
        (such as IP address and browser type) for security and reliability.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>The site is not directed to children under 13, and I don't knowingly collect their information.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted here with an updated date.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about your information, or want it deleted? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
